Mocha LineageOS 21 patch set
===========================

Patch files are grouped by their LineageOS source project. Keep each patch in
the directory matching its repository path, for example:

  frameworks/av/*.patch
  frameworks/base/*.patch
  system/core/*.patch

File names follow `NNNN-<short-slug>.patch`, where NNNN is the position of the
patch inside its project directory and the slug summarises the change (it is
the same wording used in the commit subject of the upstream project). Scripts
glob for `*.patch` and sort by path, so the numeric prefix alone decides the
apply order inside a project.

Run these scripts from any directory; they locate the source root relative to
their own location:

  device/xiaomi/mocha/patches/check.sh
  device/xiaomi/mocha/patches/install.sh
  device/xiaomi/mocha/patches/uninstall.sh

check.sh checks patches in sorted order against a temporary Git index, so
dependent patches are checked as a series without changing source files or the
real Git index. install.sh applies the same ordered series and rolls back only
patches it applied if an error occurs. uninstall.sh reverses only patches that
match this patch set, in reverse order; it never runs git checkout or git clean.

If a patch conflicts, inspect the source revision and patch intent before
editing it. Do not resolve conflicts by discarding unrelated source changes.

Every patch in this directory applies cleanly, in sorted order, to a pristine
checkout of the LineageOS 21 source tree this device tree targets.


Removed entries and why
-----------------------

Patches whose target change is already present upstream were dropped, because
they blocked a forward application of the series while contributing nothing.
None of the files below exist in this directory any more; the names are kept
only so that an older build log can still be matched:

* frameworks/av/0032-omx-bqhelper...patch.disabled targeted bqhelper files that
  no longer exist in this LineageOS 21 checkout.
* frameworks/av/0034...patch was a 2017 Qualcomm patch for
  OMXNodeInstance::freeNode and was never applied by install.sh.
* hardware/lineage/interfaces/0001, 0003, 0004 were already fully present in
  the checked-out LineageOS 21 source; verified line by line against HEAD.
* hardware/lineage/interfaces/0002...patch.disabled was superseded by the same
  upstream changes.
* packages/modules/adb/0001-hidl-transport...patch.disabled (the earlier HIDL
  rewrite attempt) is superseded by the legacy FunctionFS implementation
  already present in the checked-out source. The currently applied adb fix is
  `0001-adb-fix-legacy-functionfs-offline-transport-detached.patch`, which is
  a different change: it stops the legacy transport from reporting the USB
  endpoint as detached while the host is still probing it.


Note on frameworks/av/0041
--------------------------

The upstream Qualcomm commit assumed the Mutex::Autolock in
OMXNodeInstance::freeNode() was acquired before the mActiveBuffers check. In
this tree the check does not exist yet, so the patch could only be applied in
reverse. It has been regenerated from the actual tree difference: it now
inserts the mActiveBuffers free before the lock is taken, which is the same
end state that was built and tested on the device.
